# 3. CRITICAL DEVELOPMENT RULES

Follow these rules throughout development.

1. Build the application, not just its visual representation.
2. Implement all major navigation routes.
3. Every form must have validation.
4. Every important operation must have loading, success and failure states.
5. Persist application data in PostgreSQL when the database is configured.
6. Use development seed data when real infrastructure is unavailable.
7. Clearly distinguish simulated features from real integrations.
8. Never fabricate DNS verification, email delivery, spam scanning or payment success.
9. Never expose API keys, passwords, tokens or private DKIM keys in frontend code.
10. Never allow one organisation to access another organisation's data.
11. All administrative operations must enforce server-side permissions.
12. Use reusable components rather than duplicating entire screens.
13. Preserve existing project configuration and working code when modifying an existing project.
14. Do not replace Next.js with another framework.
15. Do not use JavaScript where TypeScript can be used.
16. Do not leave buttons without working actions.
17. Do not create dead navigation links.
18. Do not use Lorem Ipsum.
19. Do not stop after building the dashboard.
20. Complete the application incrementally and verify each module.

If a feature requires external infrastructure that is unavailable, implement its integration interface and a clearly labelled development mode.

